{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #85: declared status 'open'. Formalized: yes. Let $n\\geq 4$ and $f(n)$ be minimal such that every graph on $n$ vertices with minimal degree $\\geq f(n)$ contains a $C_4$. Is it true that, for all large $n$, $f(n+1)\\geq f(n)$? Current best: The function $f(n)$ is a reformulation of the Ramsey number $R(C_4,K_{1,n})$, in that\\[R(C_4,K_{1,n})=\\min\\{ m : f(m)\\leq m-n\\}\\]and\\[f(n)=\\min\\{ m : m\\geq R(C_4, K_{1,n-m})\\}.\\]The behaviour of this Ramsey number more generally is [552]. Prize: no. OEIS: A006672. Tags: graph theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_b1a3064da5d7038c264c30fd8beb06d6eaf252c8371eb4fb5e532e1744023b76","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:85","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_882d65f4a6b1985e","object_root":"sha256:590b37767bdf91766d3bcbb442f2e5a7a8f2362216a959e587ea12b9175fe36b","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:85"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schema":"